1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,440
<i>These two methods didn't work.</i>
<i>What the hell should I do now?</i>

2
00:00:03,520 --> 00:00:04,920
<i>"If there be one cursed by misfortune,</i>

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:06,880
<i>then must another of good fortune</i>
<i>be sought out."</i>

4
00:00:06,960 --> 00:00:10,040
"The one of fortune must have
the moon as their ruling celestial body."

5
00:00:10,120 --> 00:00:11,880
- Yo, bro!
- Shit!

6
00:00:11,960 --> 00:00:13,160
Where did you come from?

7
00:00:13,240 --> 00:00:16,920
From now on,
I'll pick you up for university every day.

8
00:00:18,040 --> 00:00:19,360
- Deal, okay?
- Hey!

9
00:00:40,280 --> 00:00:43,680
Wow, you're getting better than me now.

10
00:00:43,760 --> 00:00:45,800
You could become a basketball player
when you grow up.

11
00:00:45,880 --> 00:00:46,960
Really, Dad?

12
00:00:47,040 --> 00:00:49,520
Of course.
Come on. Let's do it one more time.

13
00:00:52,960 --> 00:00:53,800
Ouch!

14
00:01:05,160 --> 00:01:06,280
Great job, son.

15
00:01:06,360 --> 00:01:08,160
No matter how many times we fall…

16
00:01:08,240 --> 00:01:10,640
- We have to get back up again.
- We have to get back up again.

17
00:01:24,800 --> 00:01:25,720
Hello?

18
00:01:25,800 --> 00:01:27,360
Are you done yet?

19
00:01:27,440 --> 00:01:28,720
Yeah, I'm done.

20
00:01:28,800 --> 00:01:31,000
<i>Hurry up. I booked a car already.</i>

21
00:01:31,600 --> 00:01:33,240
Something unlucky might happen
if you're alone.

22
00:01:33,320 --> 00:01:34,280
<i>Fine. Got it.</i>

23
00:01:39,400 --> 00:01:42,960
<i>Seriously, why are you</i>
<i>fussing over me so much?</i>

24
00:01:43,680 --> 00:01:44,560
Well…

25
00:01:45,360 --> 00:01:49,480
You just got hurt,
so I was worried about you.

26
00:01:49,560 --> 00:01:50,480
<i>Really?</i>

27
00:01:50,560 --> 00:01:52,800
- Yeah.
- Whoa, look. The comments are pouring in.

28
00:01:54,560 --> 00:01:56,040
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

29
00:01:59,360 --> 00:02:01,920
I know why you approached me now.

30
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:03,040
Huh?

31
00:02:03,680 --> 00:02:05,480
You do?

32
00:02:11,480 --> 00:02:14,000
It's because you wanted
to make your ex jealous, right?

33
00:02:14,600 --> 00:02:15,480
Huh?

34
00:02:15,560 --> 00:02:17,680
You saw that Krit and I
are in the same faculty,

35
00:02:17,760 --> 00:02:20,160
so you're using me to get back at your ex.

36
00:02:20,960 --> 00:02:22,120
That's not true.

37
00:02:22,200 --> 00:02:23,840
I've never thought of doing that.

38
00:02:23,920 --> 00:02:25,200
I have my own reasons.

39
00:02:27,520 --> 00:02:30,440
Then what is it?

40
00:02:31,040 --> 00:02:32,720
Well, I…

41
00:02:33,680 --> 00:02:34,640
Just tell me.

42
00:02:35,520 --> 00:02:36,800
I…

43
00:02:38,960 --> 00:02:40,400
I…

44
00:02:45,160 --> 00:02:46,200
Hello?

45
00:02:46,280 --> 00:02:48,120
<i>Hello. Did you book a ride?</i>

46
00:02:48,200 --> 00:02:50,360
<i>You can come down now.</i>
<i>Traffic is getting heavy.</i>

47
00:02:52,720 --> 00:02:53,960
The car's here.

48
00:02:54,040 --> 00:02:55,000
Let's go now.

49
00:02:55,080 --> 00:02:57,640
You still haven't told me…

50
00:03:50,720 --> 00:03:52,320
Are you feeling any better?

51
00:03:52,400 --> 00:03:54,000
Well, a little.

52
00:03:55,440 --> 00:03:57,160
We're here.

53
00:03:59,120 --> 00:04:02,240
So, are you going to tell me
what your reason is?

54
00:04:03,760 --> 00:04:05,160
You're obsessed with this, aren't you?

55
00:04:05,240 --> 00:04:06,640
- Come on. Go to class.
- Wait.

56
00:04:07,840 --> 00:04:09,040
Are you coming to my class?

57
00:04:09,120 --> 00:04:10,720
Your faculty is over there.

58
00:04:11,720 --> 00:04:14,240
Oh, right.

59
00:04:14,880 --> 00:04:18,040
Don't forget that we're meeting
to work on the report this evening.

60
00:04:18,760 --> 00:04:19,600
Yeah.

61
00:04:30,760 --> 00:04:31,840
What's Rin doing here?

62
00:04:32,880 --> 00:04:34,240
Did he come to see me?

63
00:04:35,520 --> 00:04:37,680
Can't you see who Rin came here to meet?

64
00:04:39,360 --> 00:04:41,720
I don't know what you two are planning,

65
00:04:42,320 --> 00:04:44,040
but if you try to hurt Rin,

66
00:04:44,120 --> 00:04:45,640
I won't let you get away with it.

67
00:05:01,800 --> 00:05:02,640
What's going on?

68
00:05:08,120 --> 00:05:09,080
I think…

69
00:05:10,680 --> 00:05:12,840
I'm starting to believe what you told me.

70
00:05:13,440 --> 00:05:16,440
That Rin is dating him
just to get back at me.

71
00:05:17,200 --> 00:05:18,640
I don't feel good…

72
00:05:21,120 --> 00:05:22,600
about Rin dating that guy.

73
00:05:24,960 --> 00:05:29,560
Grass is not the strongest plant,

74
00:05:30,440 --> 00:05:37,200
but it is one of the toughest plants
in nature.

75
00:05:40,080 --> 00:05:42,640
If you don't stop staring at me,
I'll punch you.

76
00:05:47,320 --> 00:05:50,320
So you approached me
to make Krit jealous, right?

77
00:05:52,840 --> 00:05:53,680
Hey.

78
00:05:54,360 --> 00:05:56,240
I told you that's not true.

79
00:05:57,760 --> 00:05:59,760
Then what's your reason? Just tell me.

80
00:06:01,160 --> 00:06:02,520
I have my own reasons, okay?

81
00:06:04,760 --> 00:06:06,000
Then tell me.

82
00:06:08,160 --> 00:06:09,680
I'll tell you eventually.

83
00:06:12,600 --> 00:06:14,240
Just get back to the report.

84
00:06:14,760 --> 00:06:16,000
We brought so many books.

85
00:06:28,040 --> 00:06:33,960
Grass may not grow particularly tall.

86
00:06:34,760 --> 00:06:36,160
Finally, we're done.

87
00:06:38,600 --> 00:06:40,160
I'll send the file right away.

88
00:06:41,640 --> 00:06:42,480
Okay.

89
00:07:00,400 --> 00:07:03,720
Now all that's left is the presentation.
I'll divide the parts for us.

90
00:07:04,680 --> 00:07:05,520
Huh?

91
00:07:05,600 --> 00:07:07,800
No. You do the presentation.

92
00:07:07,880 --> 00:07:11,440
We can't do that. The professor said
everyone in the group has to present.

93
00:07:11,520 --> 00:07:12,680
Don't you remember?

94
00:07:16,120 --> 00:07:17,000
I won't do it.

95
00:07:17,680 --> 00:07:18,880
I'm embarrassed.

96
00:07:18,960 --> 00:07:19,800
Huh?

97
00:07:20,400 --> 00:07:22,720
No, you have to speak.

98
00:07:22,800 --> 00:07:27,200
This project is graded in two parts,
the written report and the presentation.

99
00:07:29,760 --> 00:07:32,440
I won't let us lose the presentation.

100
00:07:33,240 --> 00:07:35,800
No matter what, you have to present.

101
00:07:37,400 --> 00:07:38,560
No way!

102
00:07:39,560 --> 00:07:42,800
Air-purifying plants
can absorb toxins from the air

103
00:07:42,880 --> 00:07:46,240
through photosynthesis and gas exchange.

104
00:07:46,320 --> 00:07:49,120
They take in carbon dioxide
and release oxygen,

105
00:07:49,200 --> 00:07:52,640
gradually improving air quality.

106
00:07:52,720 --> 00:07:55,720
Also, don't forget
that placement is important.

107
00:07:55,800 --> 00:07:58,200
They should be placed
where there's sunlight or indirect light

108
00:07:58,280 --> 00:08:00,240
so they can photosynthesize efficiently.

109
00:08:00,320 --> 00:08:03,360
This allows the leaves to absorb toxins
and release oxygen.

110
00:08:03,960 --> 00:08:06,880
By surviving anywhere,
grass can improve its own value.

111
00:08:07,480 --> 00:08:09,280
- Thank you.
- Bravo!

112
00:08:09,360 --> 00:08:10,720
Great job!

113
00:08:12,160 --> 00:08:13,040
Well done.

114
00:08:13,640 --> 00:08:15,520
Okay. Next pair, please.

115
00:08:18,520 --> 00:08:19,600
Let's go.

116
00:08:27,480 --> 00:08:31,560
Grass is a small plant
that many people may overlook.

117
00:08:31,640 --> 00:08:36,480
But in fact, it is one
of the toughest living things in nature.

118
00:08:36,559 --> 00:08:39,039
It may not grow outstandingly tall,

119
00:08:39,120 --> 00:08:43,760
but what makes it special
is its ability to survive.

120
00:08:44,360 --> 00:08:48,640
Grass has its growing point
very close to the ground,

121
00:08:48,720 --> 00:08:54,560
which allows it to recover
even after being cut or stepped on.

122
00:08:55,160 --> 00:08:58,160
Is there anything
you'd like to add, Khobfa?

123
00:09:04,920 --> 00:09:06,000
Well…

124
00:09:10,920 --> 00:09:12,000
Well…

125
00:09:16,080 --> 00:09:17,480
Please give me a second.

126
00:09:20,120 --> 00:09:21,640
Relax, okay?

127
00:09:22,400 --> 00:09:24,800
You can do this. Don't overthink it.

128
00:09:27,520 --> 00:09:31,840
Just imagine you're telling a story
to someone you love.

129
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:39,080
So, does your group
have anything else to add?

130
00:09:40,120 --> 00:09:40,960
Yes.

131
00:09:48,640 --> 00:09:51,120
RELATED STUDIES

132
00:09:52,680 --> 00:09:57,680
<i>Just imagine you're telling a story</i>
<i>to someone you love.</i>

133
00:10:02,920 --> 00:10:04,240
Grass…

134
00:10:15,480 --> 00:10:18,280
does not always grow
in the best conditions.

135
00:10:18,360 --> 00:10:22,440
No one takes care of it
or pays attention to it.

136
00:10:23,480 --> 00:10:25,640
But every time it falls,

137
00:10:25,720 --> 00:10:28,760
it still manages
to stand back up on its own.

138
00:10:29,520 --> 00:10:30,800
Sometimes,

139
00:10:32,160 --> 00:10:36,520
true strength may simply mean surviving

140
00:10:36,600 --> 00:10:39,080
in a world that has never been kind to us,

141
00:10:39,680 --> 00:10:43,360
just like grass that may seem worthless

142
00:10:44,400 --> 00:10:47,440
but still finds its own way to grow.

143
00:11:05,240 --> 00:11:06,600
GRASS GENETICS AND STRENGTH

144
00:11:17,960 --> 00:11:19,320
- Yay!
- Yay!

145
00:11:24,240 --> 00:11:25,120
How was it?

146
00:11:25,200 --> 00:11:27,520
You got praised by the professor,
and now you don't know how to act?

147
00:11:27,600 --> 00:11:29,160
You should thank me.

148
00:11:29,240 --> 00:11:31,800
I told you to end it on a strong note.

149
00:11:32,400 --> 00:11:33,840
I'm not used to this.

150
00:11:35,880 --> 00:11:38,520
That's how it is. See? I told you.

151
00:11:38,600 --> 00:11:41,240
Everyone does well
when they're with me, kiddo.

152
00:11:41,920 --> 00:11:43,480
Damn, you're bragging so much.

153
00:11:45,400 --> 00:11:46,680
Come to think of it,

154
00:11:47,400 --> 00:11:51,320
you look really good
when you put your mind to something.

155
00:11:52,600 --> 00:11:53,640
What?

156
00:11:53,720 --> 00:11:57,120
Huh? Don't you know?

157
00:11:57,200 --> 00:11:59,720
When someone is truly focused
on doing something,

158
00:11:59,800 --> 00:12:01,640
they look incredibly attractive.

159
00:12:05,320 --> 00:12:06,440
You're exaggerating.

160
00:12:07,160 --> 00:12:08,920
Go home already. I'm going to sleep.

161
00:12:14,720 --> 00:12:15,680
Go home already.

162
00:12:17,120 --> 00:12:17,960
Hey!

163
00:12:19,520 --> 00:12:20,560
Come on.

164
00:12:23,360 --> 00:12:25,000
Are you sure you can stay alone?

165
00:12:25,080 --> 00:12:26,600
What kind of question is that?

166
00:12:26,680 --> 00:12:28,080
I've always lived alone.

167
00:12:28,160 --> 00:12:29,280
Go home already.

168
00:12:39,720 --> 00:12:41,280
Jeez.

169
00:12:49,520 --> 00:12:50,760
Hey.

170
00:12:51,440 --> 00:12:52,440
What are you doing?

171
00:12:53,040 --> 00:12:54,280
Go home already.

172
00:13:03,880 --> 00:13:05,640
Fine. I'll go.

173
00:13:15,040 --> 00:13:16,600
Be careful, okay?

174
00:13:17,200 --> 00:13:18,040
Yeah.

175
00:13:30,520 --> 00:13:31,640
<i>What should I do?</i>

176
00:13:32,200 --> 00:13:33,560
<i>Whenever I'm not with him,</i>

177
00:13:33,640 --> 00:13:36,280
<i>I'm scared something unlucky</i>
<i>will happen to him again.</i>

178
00:13:36,840 --> 00:13:41,280
<i>Then you'll have to find a way</i>
<i>to stay with him 24 hours a day.</i>

179
00:13:41,360 --> 00:13:42,360
What?

180
00:13:47,800 --> 00:13:50,960
How am I supposed
to stay with him for 24 hours a day?

181
00:14:00,160 --> 00:14:01,560
Hello?

182
00:14:01,640 --> 00:14:04,080
<i>I found out you cursed me with bad luck.</i>

183
00:14:06,160 --> 00:14:07,280
Khobfa?

184
00:14:07,360 --> 00:14:10,880
<i>- Why the hell did you do that, asshole?</i>
- Khobfa? Where are you?

185
00:14:11,440 --> 00:14:12,960
I'm sorry.

186
00:14:21,360 --> 00:14:22,280
Khobfa!

187
00:14:23,960 --> 00:14:25,240
Hey!

188
00:14:26,560 --> 00:14:28,600
Hey, Khobfa!

189
00:14:31,040 --> 00:14:32,000
<i>Khobfa!</i>

190
00:14:33,600 --> 00:14:34,600
<i>Khobfa!</i>

191
00:14:35,480 --> 00:14:36,480
Khobfa!

192
00:14:36,560 --> 00:14:37,600
Khobfa!

193
00:14:41,360 --> 00:14:43,520
Khobfa!

194
00:14:43,600 --> 00:14:46,000
You're safe, right?
Nothing unlucky happened, right?

195
00:14:46,080 --> 00:14:47,480
Well, not really.

196
00:14:47,560 --> 00:14:50,960
I just got a little electric shock
from an iron

197
00:14:51,040 --> 00:14:54,360
and fell on the balcony.

198
00:14:56,200 --> 00:14:58,920
Khobfa! Those are all unlucky!

199
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:00,640
Unlucky? What the hell?

200
00:15:04,720 --> 00:15:07,000
Why did you call us here? What's going on?

201
00:15:08,560 --> 00:15:10,680
Well, I think…

202
00:15:11,480 --> 00:15:13,360
I'm going to become Khobfa's roommate.

203
00:15:13,440 --> 00:15:14,360
- Huh?
- Huh?

204
00:15:15,440 --> 00:15:16,760
Can you at least give us a reason?

205
00:15:19,080 --> 00:15:20,280
I can't tell you yet.

206
00:15:20,360 --> 00:15:21,200
What?

207
00:15:22,600 --> 00:15:24,280
Oh, I know.

208
00:15:25,920 --> 00:15:27,800
You're trying
to make your ex jealous, right?

209
00:15:27,880 --> 00:15:28,800
Huh?

210
00:15:28,880 --> 00:15:32,200
You saw Krit flirting with Mochi,
and you couldn't stand it.

211
00:15:33,760 --> 00:15:36,240
- That has to be it.
- I think so too.

212
00:15:36,320 --> 00:15:37,960
- I don't think so.
- It is!

213
00:15:38,040 --> 00:15:39,680
Good job, my friend.

214
00:15:58,400 --> 00:16:00,560
Let me be your roommate, Khobfa.

215
00:16:00,640 --> 00:16:01,480
What?

216
00:16:01,560 --> 00:16:03,600
My friend suddenly told me
to find somewhere else to live.

217
00:16:03,680 --> 00:16:05,440
The owner of our current place
wants the house back.

218
00:16:05,520 --> 00:16:06,520
Can I stay for a while?

219
00:16:06,600 --> 00:16:08,000
No.

220
00:16:08,960 --> 00:16:10,560
Come on.

221
00:16:10,640 --> 00:16:12,200
Please help me.

222
00:16:12,280 --> 00:16:14,400
I really don't know where else to go.

223
00:16:14,480 --> 00:16:15,840
It happened so suddenly.

224
00:16:16,440 --> 00:16:18,320
Why don't you stay
with one of your friends?

225
00:16:18,920 --> 00:16:23,200
All my friends have gone back home,
but I don't have a home in Bangkok.

226
00:16:23,280 --> 00:16:24,640
Please.

227
00:16:24,720 --> 00:16:25,640
How about this?

228
00:16:25,720 --> 00:16:27,160
I'll help you with all your work.

229
00:16:27,240 --> 00:16:29,320
Whatever assignments you have,
I'll help you with everything.

230
00:16:30,640 --> 00:16:31,720
No.

231
00:16:35,320 --> 00:16:36,440
Why?

232
00:16:38,280 --> 00:16:39,640
I don't want a roommate.

233
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:44,720
You're so heartless!

234
00:16:47,280 --> 00:16:48,720
What now?

235
00:16:48,800 --> 00:16:50,440
We already worked together on the project.

236
00:16:51,040 --> 00:16:52,960
From now on, can you stop bothering me?

237
00:17:02,680 --> 00:17:03,680
Damn.

238
00:17:06,560 --> 00:17:09,040
Hey, be kind to me, okay?

239
00:17:11,760 --> 00:17:13,800
TOP 5 FINALISTS
PITCHING BUSINESS MODEL COMPETITION 2026

240
00:17:13,880 --> 00:17:16,640
Hey, your name is on it.

241
00:17:18,400 --> 00:17:19,960
You made it to the next round.

242
00:17:20,680 --> 00:17:21,520
Whoa.

243
00:17:22,119 --> 00:17:23,359
MR. KRITCHAPHAT LAMCHAISREE

244
00:17:23,440 --> 00:17:25,480
Krit's name is there too.

245
00:17:31,040 --> 00:17:32,440
Wow.

246
00:17:33,120 --> 00:17:38,040
The winner gets 300,000 baht
and 20 extra points.

247
00:17:38,880 --> 00:17:40,240
That's great.

248
00:17:44,520 --> 00:17:46,080
Why don't you look happy?

249
00:17:46,160 --> 00:17:47,800
I am happy.

250
00:17:47,880 --> 00:17:50,440
But I still have to do the pitch.

251
00:17:53,200 --> 00:17:54,720
What are you afraid of?

252
00:17:54,800 --> 00:17:56,640
Look who's right beside you.

253
00:17:56,720 --> 00:17:58,440
It's me, Rin.

254
00:17:58,520 --> 00:18:00,600
I'll coach you myself. Trust me.

255
00:18:00,680 --> 00:18:01,680
Don't you remember?

256
00:18:01,760 --> 00:18:04,080
The last time I coached you,
the professor praised you.

257
00:18:04,160 --> 00:18:05,640
You'll really coach me?

258
00:18:05,720 --> 00:18:07,960
But I have one condition.

259
00:18:08,040 --> 00:18:10,160
If you win,

260
00:18:10,680 --> 00:18:11,960
let me be your roommate.

261
00:18:14,400 --> 00:18:15,480
Then…

262
00:18:17,640 --> 00:18:18,760
never mind.

263
00:18:18,840 --> 00:18:20,240
Thanks anyway.

264
00:18:20,960 --> 00:18:23,400
Hey, come on!

265
00:18:23,480 --> 00:18:25,720
I was trying to help, Khobfa!

266
00:18:28,240 --> 00:18:29,960
<i>Let's all fall asleep together tonight.</i>

267
00:18:30,520 --> 00:18:33,040
<i>We'll live stream ourselves</i>
<i>sleeping until morning.</i>

268
00:18:35,120 --> 00:18:36,280
<i>Do you want to join us?</i>

269
00:18:36,800 --> 00:18:39,280
Look. Mochi's live stream of him
holding Krit's hand last night

270
00:18:39,360 --> 00:18:40,640
had almost 30,000 viewers.

271
00:18:40,720 --> 00:18:42,200
- Seriously? That's fab!
- It was so cute!

272
00:18:42,280 --> 00:18:43,840
There was so much engagement.

273
00:18:43,920 --> 00:18:46,760
- They're so cute together, right?
- They are!

274
00:18:47,480 --> 00:18:48,880
That's annoying.

275
00:18:51,200 --> 00:18:52,400
Mochi!

276
00:18:52,480 --> 00:18:53,800
I follow you.

277
00:18:53,880 --> 00:18:55,200
Can I take a picture with you?

278
00:18:55,280 --> 00:18:57,320
- Of course.
- Sit here.

279
00:19:01,320 --> 00:19:02,320
So cute!

280
00:19:03,040 --> 00:19:05,320
One, two, three.

281
00:19:08,880 --> 00:19:09,880
Rin.

282
00:19:15,480 --> 00:19:18,000
So are we only competing for fun?

283
00:19:18,080 --> 00:19:19,400
You're not being active at all.

284
00:19:19,480 --> 00:19:20,840
That's not like you, Rin.

285
00:19:23,240 --> 00:19:24,120
Here.

286
00:19:24,200 --> 00:19:25,240
Take this.

287
00:19:25,320 --> 00:19:26,480
Maybe it'll wake you up.

288
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:31,040
I guess getting dumped
really threw you off.

289
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:33,840
Hey!

290
00:19:35,080 --> 00:19:36,320
I'm talking to you, dude!

291
00:19:36,400 --> 00:19:39,480
How dare you come all the way
to the Faculty of Fine Arts?

292
00:19:41,520 --> 00:19:43,080
It's okay, Rin.

293
00:19:43,680 --> 00:19:46,200
We'll help you.

294
00:19:46,280 --> 00:19:48,880
Don't let him beat you, Rin.
What's so great about him?

295
00:19:48,960 --> 00:19:50,440
Only good-looking.
Has plenty of followers.

296
00:19:50,520 --> 00:19:52,560
I don't understand
why women are so obsessed with him!

297
00:19:52,640 --> 00:19:55,920
When I see him, I'm going to jab him
with my pen over and over.

298
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:56,960
Right, dude?

299
00:19:57,040 --> 00:19:59,040
Rin? Where did Rin go?

300
00:19:59,120 --> 00:20:00,600
Gosh, he left ages ago.

301
00:20:00,680 --> 00:20:01,680
Ages ago?

302
00:20:01,760 --> 00:20:03,920
Come on. Just wait until I see him.

303
00:20:14,960 --> 00:20:18,000
<i>I still haven't found a way</i>
<i>to stay with him for 24 hours.</i>

304
00:20:18,080 --> 00:20:19,720
<i>What should I do?</i>

305
00:20:21,360 --> 00:20:25,400
<i>If you can't stay with him yourself,</i>
<i>then find something to represent you.</i>

306
00:20:26,440 --> 00:20:33,080
Students, did you know that plants
are also connected to human beliefs?

307
00:20:33,160 --> 00:20:34,600
Do you know clover leaves?

308
00:20:34,680 --> 00:20:35,640
Yeah.

309
00:20:35,720 --> 00:20:39,160
It is said that
out of every 10,000 clovers,

310
00:20:39,240 --> 00:20:41,800
only one has four leaves.

311
00:20:41,880 --> 00:20:46,720
That is why a four-leaf clover
is considered a symbol of good luck.

312
00:21:14,560 --> 00:21:15,800
MISSION: SAVE THE UNLUCKY ONE

313
00:21:15,880 --> 00:21:17,640
GETTING CLOSE TO THE UNLUCKY GUY

314
00:21:31,080 --> 00:21:35,640
AI, the person I accidentally cursed
won't let me be his roommate.

315
00:21:35,720 --> 00:21:36,680
What should I do?

316
00:21:37,400 --> 00:21:38,800
<i>Don't give up yet.</i>

317
00:21:38,880 --> 00:21:40,760
<i>There's even this saying.</i>

318
00:21:40,840 --> 00:21:43,560
<i>"Dripping water</i>
<i>can eventually wear away the stone."</i>

319
00:21:43,640 --> 00:21:45,920
<i>Try to keep persuading him.</i>

320
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:48,800
But I think this stone
is about to block me.

321
00:21:49,400 --> 00:21:52,760
<i>A stone can definitely block you,</i>
<i>and it can unblock you too.</i>

322
00:21:52,840 --> 00:21:54,280
<i>Keep trying.</i>

323
00:21:56,320 --> 00:21:58,680
But I called him, and he didn't answer.

324
00:21:58,760 --> 00:22:00,560
I can't contact him at all.

325
00:22:01,560 --> 00:22:04,200
<i>If you can't reach him</i>
<i>through a communication device,</i>

326
00:22:04,280 --> 00:22:06,480
<i>then go and see him yourself.</i>

327
00:22:10,440 --> 00:22:11,280
Hey!

328
00:22:11,800 --> 00:22:12,800
Hey!

329
00:22:15,680 --> 00:22:16,520
Hey!

330
00:22:18,120 --> 00:22:19,280
Pass the ball!

331
00:22:41,560 --> 00:22:42,400
Ouch!

332
00:22:42,960 --> 00:22:44,600
How the hell are you playing like that?

333
00:22:47,440 --> 00:22:48,680
Just leave the team.

334
00:22:49,280 --> 00:22:52,120
Ever since you joined,
we haven't won a single game.

335
00:22:52,200 --> 00:22:53,520
But…

336
00:22:54,080 --> 00:22:55,440
You just broke Non's arm.

337
00:22:55,520 --> 00:22:57,240
Don't you even realize that?

338
00:22:57,320 --> 00:22:59,480
You've already brought bad luck
upon your parents.

339
00:22:59,560 --> 00:23:01,520
Are you bringing bad luck
to everyone else too?

340
00:23:02,400 --> 00:23:03,480
Damn, you're just…

341
00:23:06,520 --> 00:23:07,600
Don't follow us.

342
00:23:07,680 --> 00:23:08,680
Walk slowly, okay?

343
00:23:08,760 --> 00:23:09,600
Shit.

344
00:23:09,680 --> 00:23:11,560
- Damn it.
- Are you okay?

345
00:23:12,480 --> 00:23:14,720
<i>You jinx.</i>
<i>No wonder nobody wants you around.</i>

346
00:23:14,800 --> 00:23:17,960
<i>You're freaking unlucky.</i>
<i>I heard your parents died because of you.</i>

347
00:23:18,040 --> 00:23:19,440
<i>You're such a freaking jinx.</i>

348
00:23:20,640 --> 00:23:21,640
<i>How pathetic.</i>

349
00:23:43,640 --> 00:23:45,400
<i>Why did they have to scold you like that?</i>

350
00:23:46,000 --> 00:23:47,320
It's normal.

351
00:23:47,840 --> 00:23:49,840
I've been treated like this
since I was a kid.

352
00:23:51,800 --> 00:23:54,160
Could you somehow
try not to get used to terrible things?

353
00:24:00,840 --> 00:24:02,320
Why are you here?

354
00:24:03,080 --> 00:24:05,280
To pester me
about becoming my roommate again?

355
00:24:07,120 --> 00:24:09,080
When will you let me be your roommate?

356
00:24:14,720 --> 00:24:15,600
No way.

357
00:24:17,040 --> 00:24:18,400
What's wrong with you?

358
00:24:18,480 --> 00:24:20,320
Why won't you let me be your roommate?

359
00:24:21,720 --> 00:24:23,520
You heard what they said.

360
00:24:25,280 --> 00:24:26,680
I'm a jinx.

361
00:24:41,720 --> 00:24:42,800
You know what?

362
00:24:43,880 --> 00:24:45,840
I'm actually a very lucky person.

363
00:24:46,440 --> 00:24:50,120
My friends even nicknamed me
"the lucky charm."

364
00:24:50,200 --> 00:24:52,200
So if I live with you,

365
00:24:52,280 --> 00:24:54,800
your bad luck won't be able to affect me.

366
00:24:55,840 --> 00:24:56,680
Come on.

367
00:24:57,440 --> 00:24:59,560
Let me be your roommate.

368
00:25:07,800 --> 00:25:08,760
Let's put it this way.

369
00:25:15,360 --> 00:25:19,480
If you make one shot out of five,
I'll let you be my roommate.

370
00:25:19,560 --> 00:25:22,080
Whoa. That sounds way too easy, huh?

371
00:25:22,160 --> 00:25:23,440
You have to shoot with your eyes closed.

372
00:25:23,520 --> 00:25:24,360
Huh?

373
00:25:25,080 --> 00:25:26,880
How am I supposed to do that?

374
00:25:26,960 --> 00:25:30,080
To prove that you really are lucky.

375
00:25:30,160 --> 00:25:33,280
But if you fail,
you have to stop pestering me about this.

376
00:25:34,120 --> 00:25:35,120
Here.

377
00:25:44,560 --> 00:25:45,760
Close your eyes.

378
00:26:17,040 --> 00:26:18,520
This is your last shot.

379
00:27:02,120 --> 00:27:03,200
Just as we agreed.

380
00:27:03,960 --> 00:27:05,920
Stay out of my life after this.

381
00:27:33,040 --> 00:27:35,080
<i>Hey, jinx!</i>

382
00:27:35,680 --> 00:27:39,040
<i>I heard your parents died because of you.</i>

383
00:28:20,760 --> 00:28:22,080
YOU JINX!

384
00:28:22,160 --> 00:28:24,160
Hey, jinx!

385
00:28:24,240 --> 00:28:26,000
What's up, jinx?

386
00:28:28,880 --> 00:28:31,800
I heard your parents died because of you.

387
00:28:31,880 --> 00:28:33,520
Hey? For real?

388
00:28:33,600 --> 00:28:36,880
Damn. How pathetic.
No wonder nobody wants you around!

389
00:28:38,120 --> 00:28:39,800
You're such a freaking jinx.

390
00:28:39,880 --> 00:28:41,000
Freaking jinx!

391
00:28:41,080 --> 00:28:42,120
Let's go.

392
00:28:45,120 --> 00:28:47,400
<i>- The jinx.</i>
<i>- No wonder nobody wants you around!</i>

393
00:28:47,480 --> 00:28:50,720
<i>- You're such a freaking jinx.</i>
<i>- I heard your parents died because of you.</i>

394
00:28:50,800 --> 00:28:52,600
<i>Freaking jinx!</i>

395
00:28:53,320 --> 00:28:54,760
<i>How pathetic.</i>

396
00:29:06,920 --> 00:29:09,440
<i>Thank you so much, everyone,</i>
<i>for supporting us.</i>

397
00:29:09,520 --> 00:29:15,720
<i>You can find more information</i>
<i>about Krit's birthday party on our page.</i>

398
00:29:16,280 --> 00:29:17,800
<i>We hope to see lots of you there.</i>

399
00:29:22,680 --> 00:29:24,400
Hey, say something.

400
00:29:25,360 --> 00:29:27,640
Please come and join us.

401
00:29:28,240 --> 00:29:30,040
<i>We both worked really hard on this.</i>

402
00:29:30,120 --> 00:29:32,280
<i>We hope to see everyone there.</i>

403
00:29:32,880 --> 00:29:33,920
<i>See you soon.</i>

404
00:29:34,000 --> 00:29:35,440
<i>Bye-bye.</i>

405
00:29:35,520 --> 00:29:36,360
<i>Bye-bye.</i>

406
00:29:39,000 --> 00:29:42,440
Hey, the tickets are sold out.
I'm so excited.

407
00:29:43,040 --> 00:29:45,440
Is there anyone
you especially want to invite?

408
00:29:48,040 --> 00:29:49,400
No.

409
00:29:50,720 --> 00:29:52,360
Okay then.

410
00:29:52,440 --> 00:29:54,000
Let's head back.

411
00:29:54,080 --> 00:29:55,160
Let's go.

412
00:30:00,200 --> 00:30:01,080
Hey!

413
00:30:03,880 --> 00:30:05,000
It's still here?

414
00:30:07,280 --> 00:30:08,520
What is it?

415
00:30:08,600 --> 00:30:11,280
Here. This is the model I wanted.

416
00:30:12,640 --> 00:30:15,800
I've been saving up to buy it.
Damn, I want it so much.

417
00:30:16,960 --> 00:30:18,360
I should definitely get it.

418
00:30:20,120 --> 00:30:20,960
Let's go.

419
00:30:28,360 --> 00:30:30,040
<i>You look great, Krit.</i>

420
00:30:30,120 --> 00:30:31,960
<i>Let's go with this outfit.</i>

421
00:30:32,040 --> 00:30:33,000
Thank you.

422
00:30:35,960 --> 00:30:38,120
Ms. Prae, I think we've received
everything you sent over.

423
00:30:38,200 --> 00:30:41,400
I'll hurry and send back the first draft
along with the previous clip.

424
00:30:41,480 --> 00:30:42,880
<i>Okay.</i>

425
00:30:47,680 --> 00:30:50,800
I didn't expect being an influencer
to take this much energy.

426
00:30:51,720 --> 00:30:55,560
I thought I could just film videos
and do live streams, and that's it.

427
00:30:55,640 --> 00:30:59,440
No. There's so much more to it,
as you can see.

428
00:31:11,000 --> 00:31:13,360
Come here. I'll massage you.

429
00:31:14,920 --> 00:31:15,760
Okay.

430
00:31:23,880 --> 00:31:27,200
When you're editing the clip,
try moving around a little more.

431
00:31:37,680 --> 00:31:39,080
Can you massage me too?

432
00:31:40,960 --> 00:31:44,040
Sure. Which part?

433
00:31:52,240 --> 00:31:54,120
You should get more rest too.

434
00:32:16,400 --> 00:32:18,880
I'm sorry. I don't make kissing content.

435
00:32:21,080 --> 00:32:21,920
Well…

436
00:32:23,000 --> 00:32:23,880
I…

437
00:32:24,880 --> 00:32:26,240
Well, I'm sorry.

438
00:32:28,840 --> 00:32:32,240
Thank you so much for today.

439
00:32:33,160 --> 00:32:36,720
I'll get going then.

440
00:32:37,320 --> 00:32:38,280
Okay.

441
00:32:40,640 --> 00:32:44,600
Also, make sure you actually rest today.

442
00:32:45,200 --> 00:32:46,520
I know you're busy,

443
00:32:47,040 --> 00:32:51,080
but don't forget about my birthday party.

444
00:33:01,920 --> 00:33:03,120
Hey, Rin!

445
00:33:03,200 --> 00:33:04,040
- Ohm!
- Rin!

446
00:33:04,120 --> 00:33:05,200
- Ohm, don't!
- Rin!

447
00:33:05,280 --> 00:33:06,960
- What's with you?
- Don't!

448
00:33:07,560 --> 00:33:08,600
Look at this.

449
00:33:10,520 --> 00:33:13,000
I don't get why
they had to go all out like that.

450
00:33:20,640 --> 00:33:22,600
Hey, where are you going?

451
00:33:32,720 --> 00:33:33,960
You like it, Krit?

452
00:33:35,560 --> 00:33:36,760
Yeah.

453
00:33:36,840 --> 00:33:38,400
I've been saving up to buy it.

454
00:33:39,080 --> 00:33:40,400
Then I'll buy it for you.

455
00:33:42,280 --> 00:33:44,760
I still don't know
what to get you for your birthday.

456
00:33:49,480 --> 00:33:50,480
Thank you.

457
00:34:17,639 --> 00:34:18,760
Krit.

458
00:34:23,080 --> 00:34:25,600
Everyone's here now. Are you ready?

459
00:34:34,320 --> 00:34:35,560
I'm a little nervous.

460
00:34:37,480 --> 00:34:39,159
It's my first time
doing a fan meeting like this.

461
00:34:39,239 --> 00:34:42,600
I don't know how I should act.

462
00:34:43,280 --> 00:34:46,280
Just be yourself.

463
00:34:46,360 --> 00:34:50,400
Everyone came here because they love you
and mean well to you.

464
00:35:00,600 --> 00:35:01,520
Let's go.

465
00:35:15,160 --> 00:35:18,120
- Happy birthday, Krit!
- Happy birthday, Krit!

466
00:35:23,240 --> 00:35:25,200
I'm only here to give him the present.

467
00:35:35,600 --> 00:35:37,200
They're so cute.

468
00:35:38,120 --> 00:35:39,800
Look at their chemistry!

469
00:35:39,880 --> 00:35:41,840
They're cute.

470
00:35:42,400 --> 00:35:43,760
Oh, I'm sorry.

471
00:35:44,280 --> 00:35:45,240
Hey.

472
00:36:04,160 --> 00:36:05,280
Why are you here?

473
00:36:18,880 --> 00:36:20,120
What are you doing here, Rin?

474
00:36:20,720 --> 00:36:22,520
I'm just here to give you a present,

475
00:36:23,680 --> 00:36:24,680
like I promised.

476
00:36:26,280 --> 00:36:28,120
I don't want anything from you anymore.

477
00:36:29,720 --> 00:36:31,160
Can you stop bothering me?

478
00:36:31,240 --> 00:36:32,160
Hey, Krit.

479
00:36:34,000 --> 00:36:35,120
Please hear me out.

480
00:36:35,720 --> 00:36:37,480
This has nothing to do with anything else.

481
00:36:38,040 --> 00:36:39,840
I genuinely just wanted
to give you the present,

482
00:36:39,920 --> 00:36:42,440
so we could finally put an end to this
and have nothing left between us.

483
00:36:43,040 --> 00:36:44,440
Please take it, Krit.

484
00:36:57,080 --> 00:36:58,160
It's over.

485
00:36:59,280 --> 00:37:03,080
No matter what you do, we're already over.

486
00:37:15,280 --> 00:37:16,760
<i>Why did Rin come?</i>

487
00:37:18,760 --> 00:37:20,600
He stopped by
to give me a birthday present.

488
00:37:22,320 --> 00:37:23,680
Where is it?

489
00:37:26,200 --> 00:37:27,480
I didn't take it.

490
00:37:27,560 --> 00:37:29,040
Huh? Why?

491
00:37:30,400 --> 00:37:31,440
Well…

492
00:37:33,120 --> 00:37:34,960
If I start being nice to Rin again,

493
00:37:36,440 --> 00:37:38,080
this will never truly end.

494
00:37:43,360 --> 00:37:45,080
I'll be right back. Give me a second.

495
00:37:53,240 --> 00:37:54,280
I'm back.

496
00:37:57,560 --> 00:37:58,480
What is it?

497
00:38:05,680 --> 00:38:07,920
Here. A present from me.

498
00:38:25,920 --> 00:38:26,960
Well?

499
00:38:33,840 --> 00:38:34,880
Thank you.

500
00:38:39,840 --> 00:38:40,760
Yeah.

501
00:38:45,040 --> 00:38:46,800
I've wanted this for so long.

502
00:38:48,280 --> 00:38:49,480
You remember?

503
00:38:50,080 --> 00:38:52,400
Of course I did. So? Do you like it?

504
00:38:53,000 --> 00:38:54,040
I do.

505
00:38:55,160 --> 00:38:56,720
Happy birthday.

506
00:40:04,200 --> 00:40:05,360
<i>Hello?</i>

507
00:40:05,440 --> 00:40:06,680
Hello, Khobfa.

508
00:40:06,760 --> 00:40:07,720
What is it?

509
00:40:07,800 --> 00:40:10,040
We don't have
an elective class today, right?

510
00:40:10,120 --> 00:40:11,640
Yeah, you're right.

511
00:40:11,720 --> 00:40:14,080
Where are you now? What are you doing?
Who are you with?

512
00:40:16,880 --> 00:40:19,040
I'm alone in my room.

513
00:40:21,600 --> 00:40:23,280
I was thinking of

514
00:40:25,920 --> 00:40:27,160
hanging a plant pot here.

515
00:40:28,320 --> 00:40:29,560
Happy now?

516
00:40:29,640 --> 00:40:30,600
I'm hanging up.

517
00:40:30,680 --> 00:40:31,520
<i>Hey, wait!</i>

518
00:40:31,600 --> 00:40:32,480
RIN

519
00:40:32,560 --> 00:40:33,840
Hey…

520
00:40:34,560 --> 00:40:35,520
Jeez.

521
00:40:36,440 --> 00:40:38,400
Why do you always do such risky things?

522
00:40:43,760 --> 00:40:44,880
Rin.

523
00:40:49,440 --> 00:40:51,400
Did you come here to spite Krit again?

524
00:40:54,880 --> 00:40:56,280
What are you talking about?

525
00:40:56,880 --> 00:40:58,360
Stop pestering Krit already.

526
00:40:58,960 --> 00:41:00,080
That's right.

527
00:41:00,160 --> 00:41:01,520
What we had is over.

528
00:41:11,200 --> 00:41:13,000
It's not because I've met someone new.

529
00:41:13,080 --> 00:41:15,360
You and I just can't be together anymore.

530
00:41:19,720 --> 00:41:22,040
Having it said
straight to my face like this…

531
00:41:23,600 --> 00:41:24,800
really hurts.

532
00:41:28,480 --> 00:41:30,640
But I'm not here to pester you.

533
00:41:31,240 --> 00:41:35,720
Then why did you come here
if that's not what you were thinking?

534
00:41:38,000 --> 00:41:39,600
You've got it all wrong.

535
00:41:44,600 --> 00:41:46,440
Rin didn't come here to see you.

536
00:41:47,480 --> 00:41:48,960
He came to see me.

537
00:42:17,200 --> 00:42:19,240
Thanks for what you did earlier.

538
00:42:31,880 --> 00:42:33,240
And this is for you.

539
00:42:43,240 --> 00:42:44,880
Why do you always draw this?

540
00:42:46,680 --> 00:42:48,040
It's a four-leaf clover.

541
00:42:48,880 --> 00:42:50,160
They say that

542
00:42:50,760 --> 00:42:53,680
out of ten thousand clover leaves,
only one will have four leaves.

543
00:42:54,280 --> 00:42:56,520
That's why it represents good luck.

544
00:42:56,600 --> 00:42:59,800
So I wanted to draw it
for someone I wanted to have good luck.

545
00:43:18,640 --> 00:43:20,320
And this is your handkerchief.

546
00:43:24,440 --> 00:43:27,840
My idea helps people play.

547
00:43:30,040 --> 00:43:31,320
People play?

548
00:43:34,920 --> 00:43:36,320
I'd rather go with "simple."

549
00:43:38,680 --> 00:43:41,280
<i>Anyone who hasn't come</i>
<i>to Krit's birthday party yet,</i>

550
00:43:41,360 --> 00:43:43,120
<i>there's still time to join us.</i>

551
00:44:00,240 --> 00:44:02,000
I'm really grateful.

552
00:44:02,720 --> 00:44:04,880
I'm sorry for disturbing you.

553
00:44:05,480 --> 00:44:07,960
But from now on,
I won't bother you anymore.

554
00:44:15,920 --> 00:44:17,040
Wait.

555
00:44:23,000 --> 00:44:26,600
Let's say this clover brings you luck.

556
00:44:28,120 --> 00:44:28,960
What?

557
00:44:33,600 --> 00:44:35,200
I'll give you one more chance

558
00:44:36,120 --> 00:44:38,080
to shoot the basketball
with your eyes closed.

559
00:44:40,280 --> 00:44:42,040
If you make the shot,

560
00:44:43,240 --> 00:44:45,400
I'll let you be my roommate.

561
00:44:48,080 --> 00:44:49,440
You said it.

562
00:45:04,440 --> 00:45:06,440
How can you make the shot
holding the ball like this?

563
00:45:25,000 --> 00:45:26,280
Close your eyes.

564
00:45:52,320 --> 00:45:53,160
Hey.

565
00:45:54,880 --> 00:45:55,720
Did it go in?

566
00:46:00,560 --> 00:46:01,760
It did.

567
00:46:02,600 --> 00:46:03,560
Seriously?

568
00:46:04,320 --> 00:46:07,000
Yes! Awesome!

569
00:46:14,640 --> 00:46:16,040
Yo, my roommate!

570
00:46:18,760 --> 00:46:20,840
But you have to promise me something.

571
00:46:21,520 --> 00:46:23,560
If anything unlucky happens,

572
00:46:23,640 --> 00:46:25,640
you have to move out right away.

573
00:46:26,240 --> 00:46:27,160
Okay.

574
00:46:30,920 --> 00:46:31,880
- Deal!
- Deal!

575
00:46:34,120 --> 00:46:35,920
Then I'll go home
and pack my things today.

576
00:46:36,000 --> 00:46:37,120
I'll move in tomorrow.

577
00:46:39,680 --> 00:46:41,280
Hey, here you are.

578
00:46:57,720 --> 00:46:58,960
<i>Did it go in?</i>

579
00:47:35,400 --> 00:47:36,720
Whatever happens, happens.

580
00:47:37,240 --> 00:47:40,520
Finally having a roommate
might actually be nice.

581
00:47:43,880 --> 00:47:44,840
Right?

582
00:47:56,480 --> 00:47:57,680
SEARCH PEOPLE

583
00:47:57,760 --> 00:47:58,960
FOLLOW REQUESTS

584
00:48:02,120 --> 00:48:03,600
FOLLOW BACK

585
00:48:07,880 --> 00:48:09,800
FOLLOWING

586
00:48:19,480 --> 00:48:22,520
<i>You usually prefer being alone. Why did</i>
<i>you agree to let Rin be your roommate?</i>

587
00:48:22,600 --> 00:48:25,840
<i>You said things between you were over,</i>
<i>so make sure they really are.</i>

588
00:48:25,920 --> 00:48:27,760
What about you? Do you like Rin?

589
00:48:29,160 --> 00:48:30,360
<i>Whenever you're with me,</i>

590
00:48:30,440 --> 00:48:32,320
<i>all the unlucky things that happen</i>
<i>seem so small.</i>

591
00:48:32,400 --> 00:48:33,880
<i>I really mean that.</i>

592
00:48:33,960 --> 00:48:35,640
<i>You can stand on your own now.</i>

593
00:48:35,720 --> 00:48:38,280
<i>Show Rin that you can do</i>
<i>just fine without him.</i>

594
00:48:38,360 --> 00:48:41,600
<i>Just wait and see whether Krit or Khobfa</i>
<i>will be the one who wins.</i>

595
00:48:41,680 --> 00:48:44,240
<i>I'll do my best.</i>
<i>I promise I won't let you down.</i>

596
00:48:44,320 --> 00:48:45,440
<i>Good luck.</i>
